}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Hesperia}}|area_km2=28003.37|population_census=2,369,634|population_census_year=[[2025 Baliscan census|2025]]|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[w:Mediterranean Lingua Franca|Sabir]], [[Baliscano]], [[w:Judaeo-Spanish|Ladino]] and [[Mozbayani]]|cctld=.ksa|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|mapsize=280px|population_census_rank=20th}}'''Cassiná''' (from {{Langx|crq|Katésinát|4=fire water}}), alternatively spelled '''Cassina''', is a mountainous coastal [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of the [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Hesperia]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders [[tba]] to the north, [[Aethiopian Ocean]] to the east, [[La Serranía]] to the south, and [[tba]] to the west. The administrative seat and most populous commune within the region is [[Lugüetas]].

The climate of Cassiná is relatively similar to the meteorological conditions of [[Southwest Lurandia]]. The high areas of the region receive more rain than the coastal areas, which gradually led to the growth of temperate [[W:Cloud forest|cloud forests]]. Temperatures remain stable throughout the year, with the highest during the summer. The phenomenon of horizontal rain is very important in it [[Fortalesa Ecological Park]], where the water contained in the mists is deposited, creating a dense laurel forest.

Cassiná is the ?th-largest region by area, with an area of {{convert|28003.37|km2}}, and is the 20th-most populous, with an recorded population of 2,369,634 people in 2025. The majority of Cassiná's residents live in the metropolitan area of Lugüetas, which is also the regional center of transportation, business, and industry located in the [[Taro Valley]]. 

